# Line endings.
#
# Git already stores text as LF, but on Windows core.autocrlf=true converts it
# to CRLF on checkout. Prettier's default endOfLine is lf, so a fresh checkout
# left every file failing `npm run format:check` while looking unchanged in a
# diff — and produced a "LF will be replaced by CRLF" warning on every commit.
#
# `eol=lf` overrides autocrlf for this repository, so the working tree matches
# what is stored and what the formatter expects, on every platform. Fixing it
# in the repository rather than in one machine's git config means a clone does
# the right thing without anyone being told.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never translated, never diffed as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
